  "final_output_contracts": {
    "existing_budget": "Backward-compatible configurable main_slots plus total_budget-main_slots small slots; output is not reduced to four.",
    "main3_small1": "Area-ranked main top3 plus one peak-difference-ranked small candidate. The internal small pool is capped at peak top4. Small expansion precedes NMS; rejected candidates are refilled only from that bounded pool.",
    "main2_small2": "Area-ranked main top2 plus two peak-difference-ranked small candidates. The internal small pool is capped at peak top4. Small expansion precedes NMS; rejected candidates are refilled only from that bounded pool.",
    "internal8_to4": "Build an internal pool of area top4 main boxes and peak-difference top4 expanded small boxes without pre-NMS. Sort the unified pool by integer key (-peak_difference,-area,+component_label), then greedily accept in that order when IoU<=nms_iou against every accepted box, continuing after rejection until four outputs or pool exhaustion. A high-peak small box can therefore replace a conflicting main box. This requires only fixed-width comparators, a four-entry accepted set and IoU logic."
  },
  "selection_contract": "Main branch exactly keeps area>=main_min_area components sorted by (-area,label), capped at main_slots. The experimental branch only considers small_min_area<=area<=small_max_area. In square mode it center-expands to minimum_small_box. In perspective mode, components whose center_y reaches perspective_y_threshold use a top-anchored perspective_minimum_box; components above the threshold retain square expansion. Expansion occurs before NMS; after a conflict the rank scan continues to refill the fixed small slots. NMS rejects IoU>nms_iou against main and accepted small boxes. Its fixed slot allocation is total_budget-main_slots; unused main slots are not reassigned, so the per-frame count may be below the total budget.",
  "coordinate_contract": "All analysis boxes are inclusive. Source extent is [stride*xmin,stride*ymin,stride*(xmax+1)-1,stride*(ymax+1)-1], clipped.",
